      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <head>FIRE IN PERCIVAL'S FOLD.</head>
        <p>FIRE IN PERCIVAL'S FOLD.</p>
        <p>On Sunday morning sergeant Ball and P.C. Kane were on duty in Percival's-fold about one o'clock when they saw smoke issuing from a bedromi win dow in the lodging-house of James Gleeson. .The *officersburst open the door, rushed upstairs, and found the room full of smoke. The lodgers, five in number, were aroused, and as some men's clothes were on fire and the extent of the conflagration could not be ascertained it was decided to ring the fire bell. This was done, and the brigade, under the direction of Superintendent Trump., arrived on the scene, but in the meantime the flames had been ex- tinguished by the officers and the 10dger3 with water thrown from buckets. The damage was not very great.</p>
      </div>
