        <p>score. No 22. Pts. E Donaghy, Padgate 13 Albinson,SZnekton H....- ..... ....32 2 34 3 Green. Warringt0n...._.............32 32 "E J. 13," Warrington ....31 31 "C P," Warrington . 29 29 F Wright. Warrington 26 26 A Hall, Warrington .......18 2 20 A Albinson, Lower Walton ..........18 18 B. Tavlin, Warrington .....14 2 16 T Barnes, Sankey Bridges ..........14 14 J. Lee, Warrington lO 2 12 D Plinston, Warrington 12 12 J W Plinston, Warrington...._ 12 12 s'.l R," Padgate .. ............. ~..- 8 2 10 W Hewitt, Warrington ....- ..... 6 6 T P Forbes. Warrington .. It Mercer. Padgate .... 2 2 3 Ross, Penketh . 2 2 3 R Grieve, Warrington WE Kean,Warrington 2 2 We have to announce that the winner of our No. 5 Competition is Mr. B. Donaghy, Liverpool House, Padgate, to whom a Po3tal Order for ss. has been forwarded. We may mention in connection with the above competition that intending competitors may com- mence at any time, as at the end of each month the winner's scorry is concelled, while the remaining Competitors retain their points towards the next month.</p>
