      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0068" n="art0068">
        <head>idilliYON'S METHODS ARE EXACT.</head>
        <p>idilliYON'S METHODS ARE EXACT.</p>
        <p>His System of Treatment is Based , on Scientific Laws.</p>
        <p>" My discoveries," says Munyon, the founder of the Munyon System ef Medicine, "have estab. tabliahed the fact than there are specifics for cer- tain diseases which work with all the precision of natural laws. Where the chemical relations between medicines and diseases are known there can be ne :allure. Where such chemi. cal relations are not known. there _ guesswork. All the Munyon Remedies are based upon scientific knowledge derived from systematic investigation and experiment. The proof of this is to b 3 found in the thousands of chronic; and obstinate cases that have been cured after all ether schools of medicine have failed. MR. GRIFFEY S TRIBUTE TO MUNYON.</p>
        <p>Mr.—W-illi-A-m—G—rae-y-, residing at No 33,Priiscess-street„ Bristol says :—"I have been suffering from Rheumatism:7c for twenty years. I was under several dactors' care for years, but obtained no relief. I heard of Munvon'es Rheumatism Cure, and determined to give it a trial. I obtained a botle, and after taking only a few doses the pains lett me and I feel like a new man. Before takint Munyon's Rheumatism Care I could not raise my hand to my head, but lam al, right now. I gladly recorn4 mend Munyon's Rheumatism Care tl all sufferers. A separate cure for each disease. At all chemisth mostly One Shilling a vial. Personal letters to Prof. Munyon, 121, Shaftesbury- avenue, Lsndon, W.C., answered with free medical advice for any disease.</p>
