        <p>ic3 AGRICULTURAL LB—CTURB AT MOORE. 99 On Monday evening, Mr. Edwards, the lecturer appointed by the Cheshire County Council, gave another .of the series of agricultural lectures to farmers in the Institute. The chair was taken by Mr. T. J. Weir, and there was a fairly good attend- ance of those interested in agriculture. The subject was " Draining, liming, and economical manuring of grass land," and in a very interesting manner these subjects were discussed by the lecturer, and much 'useful information given. At the conclasioa questions were invited, and a discussion in which many joined, took place. s SALVATION ARNEL—PRIZE DISTRIBUTION.</p>
        <p>The annual prizes were distributed to the jiittiors of the above corps, the other evening, by Mr Henry Thornton, who spoke in glowing terms of the Army's work, and for the encouragement of the soldiors and friends present said he was jest send- ing £5O to the General, to aisist the noble effort being put forth to feed the starving, shelter the homeless, employ the workless, rescue the fallen reclaim the criminal, save the drunkard. and mis- sion the slums, &amp;c. (Applause.) A donation of £5 was also given by Mr. Thornton far the work locally. This was a very acceptable gift and was much appreciated.</p>
