        <p>DISTRICT COUNCIL .ELECTION.—TO THE ELECTORS OF THE TOWN HALL WARD. LADIES AND GENTLEM EN , The term for which you elected me three years ago having 'expired, I again seek the renewal of your confidence and -shall feel honoured by being returned as a representative for this important Ward. Being nn old resident in the district and a large ratepayer, I need not say that I take a deep interest in its welfare and during the time (nearly nine years) that I have been a repre- sentative of the ratepayers, I have always voted for all lusasures that in TN, opinion tended to Improve the condi- tion of the Township with regard to the supply of Water and as and the general sanitary arrangements. If elected for another term. I shall do my utmost in the "direction or necessary improvements, while at the same time will endeavour to keep the rates at the lowest possible 'Point consistent with efficiency. I have the honour to remain Your obedient servant. E. T. EVANS. March 3rd, 1899. • CHESHIRE COUNTY COUNCIL. TO CARTERS, FARMERS, AND TEAM OWNERS. PERSONS desirous of TENDERING for CARTING 1 MACADAM and other Materials for Main Roads,for the year ending 31st March. 1900, can obtain forms of Tender, and particulars of Material to be carted, at the County Surveyor's Office, Chester Castle, on and after Monday. the 13th instant, between 10 /I and 4 p.m., and on Saturdays between 10 a.m. and 1 p.m. Tenders to be endorsed "Tender for Carting," to be &amp;livered at the said Office on or before THURSDAY, the -30th instant. The Kain Roads Committee of the County Council do not bind themselves to accent the lowest or any Tender. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council. Chester, Bth March, 18§9.</p>
        <p>NEWTON URBAN DISTRICT COUNCIL.—TO TILE ELECTORS OF VIADUCT WARD. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,— At the request of a numerous body of the electors I have allowed myself to be nominated as a candidate for election to the representation of Viaduct Ward, owing to the retire- Inapt of Mr. I'. McMahon, through ill health. In asking you Or your support, I may state that I have been a resident amongst you for the past 40 years, and am therefore fujly acquainted with the rise and progress of the township, in which I have always taken a deep interest. As a direct rate- Payer it is my wish, as it must be yours, to see that the affairs of the township are conducted on an economical basis, 'Consistent with efficieney, and if it should please you to Bend cue to the Council as your representative. I will at all times endeavour to work for the best interests of the general COmmunity. Any suggested improvements will receive my znost careful attention, and I do not doubt that my actions In regard thereto will meet with your appreciation. Thank- ing you in anticipation for your support, I am, Your obedient servant, NATHANIEL SIDDELEY. Earle-street, Earlestown. March 1899.</p>
